From ad29ce322d8f1f25b77460b08bdc8cdb50fa0162 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nixos-kvm <nixos-kvm@localhost>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 06:58:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: x86: scale user-mode MSR_IA32_TSC reads (close rdmsr
 bypass)

Anti-detection: an RDTSC-only spoof leaves a hole -- in-guest kernel
code (anti-cheat drivers) can read the TSC directly via rdmsr(0x10),
which never VM-exits and would return the unscaled value. Apply the
same CPL/protmode gate + divisor in kvm_get_msr_common's MSR_IA32_TSC
case so both paths tell the same story.

Uses a compiled-in divisor default of 8, kept in sync with the
kvm_intel rdtsc_user_divisor module_param default (cross-module
sharing would require an export; deferred to a follow-up).

Lineage: dmfrpro's Hypervisor-Phantom zen-6.14.10-vmx.patch (x86.c
hunk). Rebased onto Linux 6.18.38.
---
 arch/x86/kvm/x86.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c b/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
index a21ebe0..e54ef60 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
@@ -4453,6 +4453,15 @@ int kvm_get_msr_common(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct msr_data *msr_info)
 			ratio = vcpu->arch.tsc_scaling_ratio;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Anti-detection: apply the same user-mode TSC scaling as the
+		 * VMX RDTSC handler so in-guest kernel rdmsr(0x10) reads can't
+		 * bypass the spoof. Compiled-in default; keep in sync with
+		 * rdtsc_user_divisor's default (kvm_intel).
+		 */
+		if (kvm_x86_call(get_cpl)(vcpu) != 0 || !is_protmode(vcpu))
+			ratio /= 8;
+
 		msr_info->data = kvm_scale_tsc(rdtsc(), ratio) + offset;
 		break;
 	}
-- 
